1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,037
LOVEMI

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:07,717
LOVEMI LOVEMI

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,377
KILL ME KILL ME

4
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,877
The music and the music.

5
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:39,257
I will admit my self.

6
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,017
The fear of fiction.

7
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,857
The truth and truth and truth.

8
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:46,097
I don't know what my life is.

9
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:48,237
I don't care about this song.

10
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:51,197
I won't say no high tension.

11
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,977
The role of the play is that.

12
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:54,217
I'm not a big fan.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,017
Love me! Love me!

14
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,180
I'm not a fighter Love me! Hey!

15
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:08,370
Love me!

16
00:01:08,453 --> 00:01:09,283
Love me! Love me!

17
00:01:09,366 --> 00:01:56,759
Love me!

18
00:01:56,842 --> 00:01:57,672
Love

19
00:01:57,755 --> 00:01:58,585
Nice to meet you, child of
Zenin, descendant of Michizane,

20
00:01:58,668 --> 00:01:59,498
cursed womb death painting,
and vessel of Sukuna.

21
00:01:59,581 --> 00:02:00,411
I guess you don't have a
greeting for me, Tengen.

22
00:02:00,494 --> 00:02:01,324
So this thing...

23
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:02,237
This person... Person... It's Tengen?

24
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,150
It's not our first time
meeting, Yuki Sukumo.

25
00:02:03,233 --> 00:02:04,063
Tell me why you closed
the Tombs of the Star.

26
00:02:04,146 --> 00:02:04,976
I was wary of you being
aligned with Kenjaku.

27
00:02:05,059 --> 00:02:05,889
I can't tell what's going on in
people's hearts, after all. Kenjaku?

28
00:02:05,972 --> 00:02:07,600
What was once Noritoshi Kamo,

29
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:11,320
the sorcerer who's currently
inhabiting Suguru Gato's body.

30
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:14,380
A net of compassion and
a rope of salvation.

31
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,564
Wasn't even trying for sarcasm.

32
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:20,077
You look nothing like how
I pictured you, Tengen.

33
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,925
Ballsy to insert himself
into the conversation.

34
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,660
Just because I'm immortal
doesn't make me ageless.

35
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,617
You'd look like this too
if you were 500 years old.

36
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:30,530
Seriously?

37
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,540
My aging has sped up.

38
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:38,152
Ever since I failed to assimilate with
the Star Plasma vessel 12 years ago,

39
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,920
my identity as an individual has vanished.

40
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:44,440
Now you can consider my
existence as the world itself.

41
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:48,540
So there wasn't actually another
Star Plasma vessel back then.

42
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:52,251
That explains why there isn't a new voice.

43
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,080
Excuse me?

44
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,140
We came here to learn Kenjaku's goal,

45
00:02:57,300 --> 00:03:00,017
and also to learn about how
to open the prison realm.

46
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,512
Could you tell us what you know about it?

47
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,040
Of course.

48
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:09,280
But I must impose one condition
first, and it's non-negotiable.

49
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:14,380
Yuta Okotsu, Yukitsukumo, and
the Cursed Womb Death Painting.

50
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:17,602
I'll need two of you three
to remain behind here.

51
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:20,360
Remain behind and guard me.

52
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,040
Guard you?

53
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:23,891
You said you're immortal.

54
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,237
Are you afraid of being
sealed or something?

55
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,261
That isn't fair.

56
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:31,236
Without telling us why or
how long we're guarding you.

57
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,880
In that case...

58
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:45,140
Let me speak of Kenjaku.

59
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:53,037
That man's objective is to force the
evolution of mankind throughout all of Japan.

60
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:58,037
I heard about that but how
does he actually intend

61
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:01,997
to do it and why didn't
Kenjaku use your barriers

62
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:05,217
back when he could to
turn everyone in Japan

63
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,997
into Jujutsu sorcerers
with idle transfiguration?

64
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:14,197
For a simple reason he lacked
the cursed energy to do so.

65
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:18,837
The cursed energy refined through
maelstrom can't return to the sorcerer.

66
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:23,017
Besides a curse technique evolving people
one at a time is far too inefficient.

67
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:29,077
So Kenjaku's new method of evolution
is to assimilate mankind with me.

68
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:35,017
But wait I thought

69
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,097
your assimilation should

70
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:38,827
only be possible with
the star plasma vessel?

71
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:46,920
Previously that was true but since
I started evolving 12 years ago,

72
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:54,475
assimilation with someone other than
the star plasma vessel is possible.

73
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,777
Even so you're only one person.

74
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:01,857
He still can't assimilate with
multiple people at once. Wrong.

75
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:05,817
Right now the image you are seeing
of me is not my actual self.

76
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:09,800
Now that I've evolved my soul
is everywhere all the time.

77
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:13,997
Like I said before the world
itself is who I am now.

78
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:18,337
People who assimilated with me would
become something more than a sorcerer.

79
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:22,237
They'd become a new creature that at the
same time is both there and not there.

80
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,117
It is because of my barrier
techniques that I was able

81
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,435
to retain my shape and reason
after I started evolving.

82
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,737
However, if mankind
were to begin evolving,

83
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,700
even if only one person
went out of control,

84
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,200
the world would end. Why?

85
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:40,522
There would be no boundaries
between individuals.

86
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,939
Evil would spread to all instantly.

87
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:46,437
The impurities of a hundred million
people would flood the world.

88
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:50,226
What happened in Tokyo would be
recreated on a worldwide scale.

89
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:53,157
What would make him want
to do something like that?

90
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,960
That, I do not know.

91
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,809
As I said, there's no telling
what's inside people's hearts.

92
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:01,680
If that's the case,

93
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:05,537
as long as you reject the
assimilation, won't everything be fine?

94
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:08,032
Now we're getting to why I need guarding.

95
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,297
Since I have evolved,

96
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:14,097
my nature is closer to that of a cursed
spirit than it is to that of a human being.

97
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:18,320
So I can be targeted by
cursed spirit manipulation.

98
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,957
Considering Kenjaku's enormous
strength as a sorcerer,

99
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:28,597
I would likely be absorbed the
moment he made contact with me.

100
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:33,562
That's why my main body is rejecting
everything in the tombs of the star right now.

101
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:35,926
That's why you need guarding?

102
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:37,910
Correct.

103
00:06:37,993 --> 00:06:40,997
Kenjaku is second only to me in
his skill with barrier techniques.

104
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:44,817
I don't know when he'll manage to break
the seal on the tombs of the star.

105
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,429
Why is this happening now?

106
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:49,057
The star plasma vessel
assimilation failed.

107
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:50,297
You've been forced to evolve,

108
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,157
so he wants to absorb you with
cursed energy manipulation.

109
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:56,580
It also seems Kenjaku has
connections to Sukuna,

110
00:06:56,920 --> 00:07:00,332
which means he's been a sorcerer
for at least 1,000 years.

111
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,040
So then, why now?

112
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:04,640
Because myself,

113
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,157
the Star Plasma Vessel,

114
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:10,820
and the Six Eyes are all connected by
fate and intertwined with each other.

115
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:16,157
Twice in the past, Kenjaku was stopped
by the Sorcerer with the Six Eyes.

116
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,077
The second time, he was thorough.

117
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,197
He killed both the Star
Plasma Vessel and the

118
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:23,157
Bearer of the Six Eyes within
a month of their birth.

119
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,070
Despite that,

120
00:07:24,153 --> 00:07:25,977
the Six Eyes and the Star Plasma Vessel

121
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:28,707
still appeared by the
day of my assimilation.

122
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,680
After that,

123
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,917
Kenjaku altered his strategy to
focus on sealing the Six Eyes

124
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,657
instead of killing him as he began
searching for the prison realm.

125
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:40,975
After all, there can't be two people
with the Six Eyes at the same time.

126
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:44,414
However, 12 years ago, something
unpredictable happened.

127
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:46,240
Toji Zenin intervened.

128
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,240
He was physically gifted
through a heavenly pact,

129
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:54,773
and he was unique among them for being
completely free from cursed energy.

130
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:00,340
Since his heavenly pact
placed him outside of fate,

131
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,736
he decided to destroy the
very fate that connected us.

132
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:08,215
Then, a young man with the power of
cursed spirit manipulation appeared.

133
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,756
Without even trying,

134
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:13,625
he now had all the necessary
pieces except for the Prison Realm.

135
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:19,780
But six years ago, the Prison Realm made
its way into Kenjaku's hands as well.

136
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,971
If Kenjaku has the Prison Realm, then
why is this Culling Game being hosted?

137
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,180
It's a warm-up before assimilation.

138
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:31,937
My assimilation with people other than
the Star Plasma Vessel is possible,

139
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:36,537
but at the moment there's a high probability
it will result in something incomplete.

140
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:41,377
The Culling Game uses the cursed energy
of the players and the boundaries formed

141
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:46,217
between the colonies in a ritual to send
this nation's people to the other side.

142
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:51,100
He probably plans to use that as a warm-up
to start their assimilation with me.

143
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,540
However, to establish that ritual,

144
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:58,380
Kenjaku should have been
forced to accept several pacts.

145
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,657
One of those pacts is that
Kenjaku is not allowed

146
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:07,505
to name himself the
Culling Game's Game Master.

147
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:10,457
Unfortunately, that's a
disadvantage to you as well,

148
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:14,080
because it means that killing
Kenjaku won't end the game.

149
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:17,640
Either all of the players must die,

150
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:21,036
or the players must all
refuse to participate and die.

151
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,877
The rules specifically
mention that nothing must

152
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,357
significantly hinder the
continuation of the Culling Game,

153
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:30,897
an insurance policy to prevent
the ritual from being stopped.

154
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:32,820
In that case... Yeah, right.

155
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:38,017
All of us need to participate
in the Culling Game,

156
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,697
and add a rule that creates
a way out of the game

157
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:43,486
for Sumiki and those
reluctant to participate.

158
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:47,867
We need to free Gojo-sensei
at the same time.

159
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:50,766
He could resolve this
all entirely on his own.

160
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:56,913
Uh, what do we do next?

161
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:00,360
First, please decide which
of you will stay behind.

162
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,430
I'll do it.

163
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:03,210
I'll stay.

164
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:04,410
Huh?

165
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:08,977
Yuji, you are absolutely going to need
the help of either Okotsu or that woman.

166
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:10,000
Noritoshi Kamo.

167
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:14,337
If Kenjaku comes, that's all the
more reason for me to guard Tengen.

168
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:18,537
I must do so because slaying him
would mean saving my younger brothers.

169
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:21,679
I'm still not finished
talking with Tengen just yet.

170
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,680
Does that sound okay, Okotsu? Yeah.

171
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:27,980
I don't want to be separated
from everyone anymore.

172
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:31,580
Thank you.

173
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,780
Now this.

174
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:39,157
This is the back of the prison realm.

175
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:43,637
If you plan to free Satoru
Gojo, you'll need it.

176
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,550
The back.

177
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:46,557
First, I've heard of it.

178
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,877
Like a back door.

179
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,317
That's right.

180
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:53,877
Before Kenjaku found it, the prison
realm was outside of my barriers.

181
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,637
Probably somewhere abroad.

182
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:59,620
I thought keeping this back sealed would.

183
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:03,617
obscure the presence of the
front, but it didn't work.

184
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:06,500
Satoru Gojo is also
sealed away within this

185
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,200
back gate. What?

186
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,017
Then let's open it and let him out!

187
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:15,540
No, the authority to open the gates rests
with the owner of the front, Kenjaku.

188
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,782
In order to break this one open,

189
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,457
you need either the inverted
spear of heaven that

190
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,997
can force the cancellation
of cursed techniques,

191
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:27,217
or something that can disrupt and cancel
out the effects of a cursed technique.

192
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,620
The black rope could

193
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:30,850
do it.

194
00:11:30,933 --> 00:11:35,160
However, twelve years ago Satoru Gojo
either sealed the inverted spear of

195
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,697
heaven abroad or destroyed it.

196
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,500
Why would you do that sensei?

197
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:43,880
And last year the black rope was
also completely frayed by Gojo.

198
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,560
What was he thinking?

199
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,095
Reminds me of Miguel.

200
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:52,497
We went to Africa looking for
some more of that black rope.

201
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:54,051
So that's where you were.

202
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,807
Please tell me you found it.

203
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:58,397
Sorry, but it was a
complete waste of effort.

204
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,817
They said it's all gone.

205
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:00,730
Huh?

206
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,600
Is there another way? There is.

207
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:07,877
Among the players participating
in the upcoming Culling Game,

208
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,725
there's a sorcerer from 1,000
years ago who calls herself Angel.

209
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:23,700
Her curse technique can extinguish
any other curse technique.

210
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:33,800
Extinguish any curse technique?

211
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,330
Yes.

212
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:40,721
And Angel's curse technique also has the
power to open the back of the prison realm.

213
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:43,114
Can you tell us where she is right now?

214
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:46,166
She's in the colony on
the east side of Tokyo.

215
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,657
The barriers of the
culling game reject me.

216
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:51,975
I'm afraid I don't have any
more information than that.

217
00:12:57,020 --> 00:12:59,432
Let's start going over things from there.

218
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,960
There are ten colonies across Japan.

219
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:04,797
They are linked together
by barriers designed to

220
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,697
ferry the country's people
over to the other side.

221
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:09,337
Crossing a river or other border.

222
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,037
acts that symbolize crossing
over to the afterlife.

223
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,557
These carry important meanings in sorcery.

224
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,875
Oh, it's like with Yasohachi Bridge.

225
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:33,920
The Jujutsu Society's barrier.

226
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,700
So is Hokkaido excluded?

227
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:36,870
It is.

228
00:13:36,953 --> 00:13:40,660
That land is already established
as a vast sacred ground.

229
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:43,788
I guess that's the
challenging land for you.

230
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:47,940
Ferry them to the other side
may sound a bit dramatic,

231
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:52,888
but everyone in Japan was cursed in
preparation for the upcoming assimilation.

232
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,660
Tell me about this ritual.

233
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
How long will it take to complete?

234
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:05,867
Depends on the culling game.

235
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,101
My guess it's over in two months.

236
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,100
It is currently 9 a .m.

237
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,573
on the 9th of November.

238
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:17,477
Nine days since the players
awakened as sorcerers,

239
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:20,148
which happened October
City around midnight.

240
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:26,200
That gives us about 10 days and 15 hours
to go before Tsumiki is forced to play.

241
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:37,797
Tengen, you said before that people
would die if they refused to participate.

242
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,710
That's right.

243
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:41,417
They get stripped of their technique, huh?

244
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:45,441
I believe that rule also applies
to any sorcerers joining in later.

245
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:50,512
If that's the case, the stripping isn't
being done by idle transfiguration.

246
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,120
It's not a pact either, because
it says stripped, not prohibited.

247
00:14:56,600 --> 00:15:00,457
So that probably means it'll be doing
something to the brain by force.

248
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:04,364
And it's better for the rules if
being stripped means death, too.

249
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:07,284
Otherwise, everyone would
refuse to participate.

250
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,460
It's just as Shoko anticipated.

251
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,217
But that also means there's no risk to

252
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:15,065
sorcerers without any
cursed technique like me.

253
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:16,867
And what'll happen to Panda?

254
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,889
Does he even have a brain?

255
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,580
About this rule,

256
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:27,917
what does it mean for the ordinary people
who are in the colony from the start?

257
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,737
It means anyone who wants will be
granted at least one chance to leave.

258
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:32,650
For real?

259
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,420
How awfully generous.

260
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:39,633
There are no stipulations in the rules
about leaving or entering colonies.

261
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:43,717
They were probably trying to stimulate
the culling game by giving players

262
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:47,918
a clear first-time goal of leaving
the colony with their lives intact.

263
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:51,417
In order to keep the players
inside for the duration.

264
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:54,117
The premise that players
entered of their own free will?

265
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,640
is extremely important.

266
00:15:56,380 --> 00:16:00,027
Eno mentioned that thing about
adjusting the barrier strength.

267
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,700
Using fundamentally in a rule?

268
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,134
Why make it confusing?

269
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,760
Is something wrong?

270
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,340
It's nothing.

271
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:20,520
Tengen, who is this Game Master?

272
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:26,020
Every individual player is
given a Shikigami called Kogane.

273
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:30,020
To be precise, Kogane
isn't the Game Master.

274
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:31,697
It's an interface.

275
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:36,180
It's best to think of the culling
game itself as the Game Master.

276
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,000
Okay, I got it.

277
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:46,600
So we can add, but we're not allowed
to eliminate any existing rules.

278
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:52,109
Maybe we'll be able to come up
with some kind of workaround.

279
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,318
How's that allowed?

280
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,360
Yeah, right.

281
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,229
It leans too heavily
on their own judgment.

282
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:02,690
No.

283
00:17:02,773 --> 00:17:06,097
You should expect a fair decision
when it comes to all challenges.

284
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,677
They're already subjecting the
players to such stringent rules.

285
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:14,289
Jujutsu Sorcery would not allow them to
show more favoritism towards Kenjaku.

286
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,838
So then, does that mean I'll
be killing people again?

287
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,300
Maybe not.

288
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,100
I have a few ideas.

289
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:29,381
We've managed to organize
our information for now.

290
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:32,051
That just leaves the roles for each of us.

291
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,440
Yuki and Choso will remain here.

292
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,955
They'll guard Tengen.

293
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:43,054
Meanwhile, I need to return to the
Zenin house to get their cursed tools.

294
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,360
Right after Gojo was sealed,

295
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:47,677
the Kamo and Zenin clans
both took their cursed

296
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:50,237
tools out of Jujutsu
High's Forbidden Vault.

297
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:53,217
However, Megumi is now the
head of the Zenin clan.

298
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,130
Who?

299
00:17:54,213 --> 00:17:55,766
I'll explain it to you later.

300
00:17:56,260 --> 00:17:59,197
So we're free to rummage through
the Zenion's forbidden vault.

301
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:00,110
That.

302
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,140
Before that, Tengen.

303
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:04,080
I know what you want.

304
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,260
It's Juzo Kumio's Atelier.

305
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:07,920
Yes, thank you.

306
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,657
Once I'm finished, I'll look for Panda.

307
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:13,177
After that, I'll help deal
with the Culling Game.

308
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:14,090
And you, Yuta?

309
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:17,717
I'll enter a colony and
participate in the Culling Game.

310
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,977
The sooner, the better.

311
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:22,557
Before Sumiki and Fushiguro enter,
I want to know as much as I can.

312
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,581
Then I'll be thoroughly prepared.

313
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,330
Thank you.

314
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,554
It'll mean acting on my own once again.

315
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,870
However,

316
00:18:30,953 --> 00:18:33,017
in order to prevent us from
clashing with each other,

317
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:36,480
and in case something does
happen to Sumiki out there,?

318
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:38,484
I'll avoid the nearby colonies.

319
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:42,557
We should be aware that the
colonies might cut off reception,

320
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:45,052
so I might be out of contact for a while.

321
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:49,936
If Sukuna appears and takes control
of me again, I need you to kill me.

322
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,288
Don't worry about that now.

323
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:55,958
It's gonna be fine.

324
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:58,789
If that happens, you
can have him kill you.

325
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,000
After I die.

326
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:03,065
Yeah, well, I'm trying
to avoid that situation.

327
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:04,570
Maki.

328
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:05,930
Right.

329
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:09,178
I want you two to meet up
with Kinji like we planned.

330
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,190
Kinji?

331
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:11,720
Kinji Hakari.

332
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,315
The third-year guy that got suspended.

333
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:17,197
We're shorthanded, so
it's all hands on deck.

334
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,357
Do whatever it takes to recruit him.

335
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:20,734
Is he strong at least?

336
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:26,217
He's a bit erratic, but if he gets into
it, he can be even stronger than I am.

337
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,418
That is impossible.

338
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:08,810
Joseph!

339
00:20:08,893 --> 00:20:10,596
I want to thank you for all the help.

340
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:12,796
Don't die out there.

341
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:22,100
Are you really crying? Shh, shh.

342
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,370
Yeah.

343
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:35,000
Uh, thanks for coming.

344
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,050
Takaba!

345
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:41,177
How long are you going
to keep doing that crap?

346
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,090
Cut it out!

347
00:20:42,173 --> 00:20:43,757
Ah, you're making me depressed.

348
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:44,900
The audience, too.

349
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:46,530
Yeah, I know.

350
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:49,000
How old are you now?

351
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,980
35 years old.

352
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:52,832
Just give it up already.

353
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:58,200
Our industry is full of late bloomers who
suddenly make it big for no good reason.

354
00:20:58,380 --> 00:20:59,660
But not a single one.

355
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,682
Out of the blue suddenly
actually became funnier.

356
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:06,797
They were already funny people
waiting patiently to be discovered.

357
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,527
That ain't the case for you.

358
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,447
Look what happened to Tokyo.

359
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,057
No one's gonna think ill of you.

360
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:14,669
Go do something you're
actually suited for.

361
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,737
I always thought you were kind of funny.

362
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:22,291
You always made me laugh.

363
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:24,600
You mean it, Ken?

364
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,180
Both you and him have the wrong idea.

365
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:31,414
There are people who ain't
funny that still make it big.

366
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:37,097
Are they one-gag comics like me, though?

367
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:38,010
Absolutely not.

368
00:21:38,093 --> 00:21:40,717
there are two types of comedians
that manage to stay big

369
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:45,417
comedians who are always funny
and comedians who can go ahead

370
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:46,557
and delude themselves into

371
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,470
believing they

372
00:21:47,553 --> 00:21:51,957
are so

373
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:55,197
which type

374
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:59,960
are you well I'd like to think
I'm 50 50 but in Actuality,

375
00:22:00,060 --> 00:22:02,178
it's probably a lot closer to 70-30.

376
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,740
50-50 or 70-30!

377
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,520
Thank you.

378
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:29,317
It's scary for you, too.

379
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:32,620
Na-zori na-kara nukau no-ho so!
